  :adr/body "# Kotoba stack performance — measured comparison and world-class gates\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted (2026-08-26). Owner ambition: **#1 in every owned domain**, but only where a versioned benchmark contract and fleet gate say so.\n\n## Context\n\nPrior answers mixed amu (compiler), kototama (tender), aiueos (OS), and legacy Rust kotoba DB numbers. Only **amu** had reproducible cross-engine evidence (`kotoba.runtime-comparison/v1`, `kotoba.performance-baseline/v1` in `orgs/kotoba-lang/amu/docs/performance.md`).\n\n2026-08-26 session ran fresh benchmarks on Apple M4 (load average 17–25, contended).\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **Superproject evidence plane:** `90-docs/performance/runs/<date>/*.json` + `performance.datoms.edn`; human summaries live in `docs/performance/` (90-docs is EDN-only).\n2. **Weekly snapshot:** update `kotoba-stack-benchmark-<date>.md` or rolling section in roadmap; pin JSON artifacts per date.\n3. **World-class gates** (honest baselines 2026-08-26):\n   - **amu native narrow kernel:** 23.62 ns vs Rust 22.64 ns = **1.04×** — competitive, not certified #1.\n   - **amu Wasm32:** 5.25× Rust — not #1.\n   - **compile cold:** ~1.95 s wasm32 — not #1; worker hit ~31 ms — viable edit loop.\n   - **kototama JVM path:** ~3.4 s per cold fact.wasm — not #1; browser path is first-class.\n   - **aiueos:** UNMEASURED — add `kotoba.os-microbench/v1` before any OS perf claim.\n4. **Regression policy:** new fleet gate `root-kotoba-stack-performance` (follow-up) compares pinned `runs/` JSON; >5% regression on quiet host blocks merge.\n5. **Certification:** use `perfgate.core/qualify` for any \"faster than LLVM/Rust\" claim (see amu `performance.md` kernel_wide section).\n\n## Consequences\n\nPositive: single place to answer \"how fast are we\"; stops citing 2024 Rust DB numbers as current stack.\nNegative: contended 2026-08-26 numbers are exploratory — re-run on quiet fleet node before marketing.\n\n## Evidence paths\n\n- `docs/performance/kotoba-stack-benchmark-2026-08-26.md`\n- `docs/performance/world-class-roadmap.md`\n- `90-docs/performance/performance.datoms.edn`\n- `90-docs/performance/runs/2026-08-26/kotoba-runtime-20260826.json`\n- `90-docs/performance/runs/2026-08-26/kotoba-compile-20260826.json`\n- amu commit `6889fa736750`\n\n## Resume\n\nNext engineering: (1) `kotoba.tender-comparison/v1`, (2) `kotoba.os-microbench/v1`, (3) fleet gate, (4) call-aware register allocator (amu `performance.md` § functions that call)."}]
